---
title: Device Care
---

Field devices encounter mud, water, biological material, heat, and limited charging. A simple care routine protects both equipment and data.

## Sanitize safely

- Turn off or lock the device and disconnect cables before cleaning.
- Use a soft microfiber cloth lightly dampened with 70% isopropyl alcohol, when permitted by the manufacturer.
- Wipe edges and crevices carefully, and allow the device to air-dry completely.
- Do not pour liquid onto the device or use ammonia-based glass cleaner, nail-polish remover, or undiluted bleach.
- Disinfect after each field session or between users on shared devices.

Always check the current cleaning instructions from your manufacturer: [Apple](https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT204172), [Google Pixel](https://support.google.com/pixelphone/answer/7530172), or [Samsung](https://www.samsung.com/us/support/answer/ANS00086342/).

## Conserve battery

Lower brightness, enable Low Power or Battery Saver mode, and close work that is not needed. Turn off Bluetooth, cellular data, Wi-Fi, or airplane-mode connections when they are not required. Limit background location access for other apps. NAHPU uses GPS when you generate a site coordinate, so continuous background location is not required. Carry a charged power bank and avoid leaving batteries in excessive heat.

## Manage connectivity and GPS

Use connectivity intentionally: download or update what you need before departure, then test NAHPU in airplane mode. Re-enable a connection only when syncing, transferring, or backing up. Grant location permission when you need to generate a site coordinate, keep a clear view of the sky when possible, and review the coordinate before saving it. Do not rely on GPS alone when local safety or collecting rules require another location record.
